NNAAMMEE
       cksum - compute and verify file checksums

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       cckkssuumm [_O_P_T_I_O_N]... [_F_I_L_E]...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Print or verify checksums.  By default use the 32 bit CRC algorithm.

       With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

       Mandatory  arguments  to  long  options are mandatory for short options
       too.

       --aa, ----aallggoorriitthhmm=_T_Y_P_E
              select the digest type to use.  See DIGEST below.

       --cc, ----cchheecckk
              read checksums from the FILEs and check them

       --ll, ----lleennggtthh=_B_I_T_S
              digest length in bits; must not exceed the max  for  the  blake2
              algorithm and must be a multiple of 8

       ----ttaagg  create a BSD-style checksum (the default)

       ----uunnttaaggggeedd
              create a reversed style checksum, without digest type

       --zz, ----zzeerroo
              end  each  output  line  with NUL, not newline, and disable file
              name escaping

   TThhee ffoolllloowwiinngg ffiivvee ooppttiioonnss aarree uusseeffuull oonnllyy wwhheenn vveerriiffyyiinngg cchheecckkssuummss::
       ----iiggnnoorree--mmiissssiinngg
              don't fail or report status for missing files

       ----qquuiieett
              don't print OK for each successfully verified file

       ----ssttaattuuss
              don't output anything, status code shows success

       ----ssttrriicctt
              exit non-zero for improperly formatted checksum lines

       --ww, ----wwaarrnn
              warn about improperly formatted checksum lines

       ----ddeebbuugg
              indicate which implementation used

       ----hheellpp display this help and exit

       ----vveerrssiioonn
              output version information and exit

   DDIIGGEESSTT ddeetteerrmmiinneess tthhee ddiiggeesstt aallggoorriitthhmm aanndd ddeeffaauulltt oouuttppuutt ffoorrmmaatt::
       sysv   (equivalent to sum --ss)

       bsd    (equivalent to sum --rr)

       crc    (equivalent to cksum)

       md5    (equivalent to md5sum)

       sha1   (equivalent to sha1sum)

       sha224 (equivalent to sha224sum)

       sha256 (equivalent to sha256sum)

       sha384 (equivalent to sha384sum)

       sha512 (equivalent to sha512sum)

       blake2b
              (equivalent to b2sum)

       sm3    (only available through cksum)

       When checking, the input should be a former output of this program,  or
       equivalent standalone program.

